function infoCw_injectToCodex()
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addCategory', 'cw_cat', 'Cosmic War'%_t, 'data/textures/icons/cw_galacticpolitics.png')

    -- Full Feature Breakdown
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'cw_cat', 'cw_cat_c0', 'Full Feature Breakdown'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a0', 'War-Oriented AI Faction Seeding'%_t, 'Primary file: data/scripts/server/factions.lua\n\nInjects and maintains faction-level war metadata for AI factions so behavior trends are less random and more identity-driven over time.\n\nTypical Stored Values:\n\n- cw_enabled\n- cw_war_bias\n- cw_diplomatic_polarity\n- Rivalry target helpers used by downstream systems.\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- AI factions feel less interchangeable.\n- Rivalries become more coherent in long campaigns.\n- Better continuity between isolated events and long-term politics.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a1', 'Sector War-Pressure Controller'%_t, 'Primary files:\n\n- data/scripts/sector/init.lua\n- data/scripts/sector/cosmicwarcontroller.lua\n\nRuns periodic sector-level scans and applies pressure to selected faction pairs when local conflict conditions align.\n\nBehavior Goals:\n\n- Encourage natural hotspot emergence.\n- Avoid spam via spacing/cooldown logic.\n- Prevent every loaded sector from escalating identically.\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Frontlines and contested regions emerge organically.\n- Different sectors can diverge into quiet vs. volatile states.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a2', 'Persistent Diplomacy Drift'%_t, 'Primary files:\n\n- data/scripts/player/init.lua\n- data/scripts/player/background/cosmicwardiplomacy.lua\n\nPeriodically evaluates random/eligible faction-pair subsets and nudges diplomacy over time.\n\nWhy it matters:\nWithout drift, diplomacy can remain too static between discrete scripted events.\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Politics evolve continuously.\n- Rivalry maintenance feels systemic, not scripted-only.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a3', 'War News / Broadcast Layer'%_t, 'Primary file: data/scripts/server/background/cosmicwarnews.lua\n\nPublishes periodic war bulletins to improve player awareness of macro conflict shifts.\n\nImplementation Style:\n\n- Collects currently hot conflicts.\n- Chooses one using stable randomization.\n- Broadcasts informational message server-wide.\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Players can react strategically to political shifts.\n- Background simulation becomes visible and actionable.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a4', 'Diplomatic Sanctions Pressure'%_t, 'Primary file: data/scripts/server/background/cosmicwardiplomaticsanctions.lua\n\nApplies sanction-like pressure behavior tied to entrenched rivalries and hostile diplomatic states.\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Wars have economic/diplomatic consequences, not only combat outcomes.\n- Political hostility influences broader strategic conditions.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a5', 'Ceasefire / Dtente Logic'%_t, 'Primary file: data/scripts/server/background/cosmicwarceasefires.lua\n\nAllows conditional de-escalation when hostility recovers and ceasefire chance criteria are met.\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Conflict cycles can resolve naturally.\n- The galaxy does not lock permanently into one escalated state.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a6', 'War Bounty Generation'%_t, 'Primary file: data/scripts/server/background/cosmicwarbounties.lua\n\nCreates time-bound bounty opportunities linked to active faction rivalries.\n\nTypical Stored Value Pattern:\n\n- Target faction ID.\n- Reward value.\n- Expiration runtime.\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Gives players direct incentives to engage with active wars.\n- Converts geopolitical state into mission-like opportunities.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a7', 'Dynamic Territory Sieges & AI Boarding'%_t, 'Primary files:\n\n- data/scripts/lib/cosmicvaultterritory.lua (via Cosmic Vault)\n- data/scripts/events/siegeevent.lua\n- data/scripts/entity/ai/trooptransport.lua\n\nAllows factions to actively conquer enemy sectors and permanently expand their borders on the Galaxy Map. By utilizing mathematically abstracted background timers, the server naturally shifts influence without keeping thousands of sectors loaded (avoiding the \"Sector Alive\" crash trap).\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Background Conquests: Contested zones have a hidden siege timer. If time runs out, the station flips ownership mathematically.\n- Physical Sieges: If a player enters a contested zone, the engine triggers a Siege Event.\n- Troop Transports: Three massive, heavily shielded AI transports will warp in and charge the defending station. If they survive the station\'s point-defense for 60 seconds (scaling up to 5 minutes based on the station\'s hull HP) at close range, they physically board and capture the station!\n- Dynamic Borders: Once a station flips ownership, the Galaxy Map influence border naturally expands.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a8', 'Cosmic Overhaul Synergy (Bridge Layer)'%_t, 'Primary bridge files:\n\n- data/scripts/lib/cosmicwareconomybridge.lua\n- data/scripts/lib/cosmicwarcaptainbridge.lua\n\nTypical wrapper targets (when present in the load stack):\nCommand prediction hooks in simulation scripts (e.g., trade, scout, travel, refine, mine, salvage variants).\n\nDesign Intent:\n\n- Emphasizes non-invasive composition over hard overwrites.\n- The original prediction path runs first.\n- The bridge applies bounded post-processing only when enabled and when the context is valid.\n- Graceful no-op fallback occurs when disabled or when missing context.\n\nHigh-Level Effect:\n\n- Command planning outputs can reflect war-heat pressure more clearly.\n- Baseline behavior is safely preserved when bridge toggles are disabled.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a9', 'Dynamic War Contracts (Missions)'%_t, 'Primary files:\n\n- data/scripts/entity/bulletinboardmissions.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_forcerecon.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_borderskirmish.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_resourcesabotage.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_interception.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_breakthrough.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_frontlinesiege.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_highvaluedefection.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_decapitationstrike.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_sector_raid.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_hunter_killer.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_resource_heist.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_distraction_carnage.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_black_box_retrieval.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_blockade_runner.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_champion_duel.lua\n- data/scripts/player/missions/cw_sensor_deployment.lua\n\nInjects custom, highly-scaled combat missions directly into Avorion\'s native Bulletin Board mission pools based on the current macro-level War Heat between the station\'s owner and their rival faction.\n\nAvailable Contracts:\n\n- War Heat > 0.15: Force Recon (Scout a hostile listening post) & Sensor Deployment (Sneak into the dead center of 3 hostile sectors).\n- War Heat > 0.25: Border Skirmish (Eliminate an enemy border patrol).\n- War Heat > 0.35: Resource Sabotage (Destroy an enemy mining operation), Resource Heist (Infiltrate and steal large quantities of resources), & Deploy Minefield (Deploy and defend a minefield).\n- War Heat > 0.45: Interception (Destroy enemy supply convoy), Breakthrough (Defend allied supply convoy), Sector Raid (Wipe out enemy infrastructure), Black Box Retrieval (Extract data from a destroyed prototype), & Propaganda Broadcast (Hack comms array).\n- War Heat > 0.60: Frontline Siege (Assault a dynamically scaled enemy FOB), Hunter Killer (Hunt a specialized fleet), & Distraction Carnage (Survive a massive 5-minute ambush).\n- War Heat > 0.80: High-Value Extraction (Holdout survival for defector), Assassinate General (Kill a high-ranking target), Supply Line Raid (Destroy logistics hubs), & Blockade Runner (Deliver supplies through a heavy blockade).\n- War Heat = 1.00: Decapitation Strike (Ultra-hard Flagship Boss), Extract POW (Rescue prisoners from a heavily guarded facility), & Champion Duel (1-on-1 duel with a scaled boss).\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a10', 'Dynamic War Events (Flashpoints)'%_t, 'Primary files:\n\n- data/scripts/player/eventscheduler.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_fleetclash.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_refugeeconvoy.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_strandedflagship.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_armsdeal.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_diplomaticsabotage.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_capital_ship_duel.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_orbital_bombardment.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_distress_beacon_trap.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_stationsiege.lua\n- data/scripts/events/cw_blockade.lua\n\nInjects new spontaneous events into Avorion\'s global event scheduler. As players explore the galaxy, they will encounter live warzones, covert operations, and distress calls directly tied to the macro political simulation.\n\nAvailable Events:\n\n- Fleet Clash (Heat > 0.60): Massive enemy strike fleets jump into active AI sectors.\n- Refugee Convoy (Heat > 0.40): Civilian freighters are ambushed by hunter fleets.\n- Stranded Flagship (Heat > 0.80): A severely damaged dreadnought boss is discovered vulnerable, with a repair fleet en route.\n- Arms Deal (Heat > 0.20): An illegal weapon transaction occurs, dropping high-rarity turrets if interrupted.\n- Diplomatic Sabotage (Heat > 0.20): Extremists attack a peace envoy. Saving the envoy provides massive reputation.\n- Capital Ship Duel: Two massive rival dreadnoughts warp in and engage in a fight to the death.\n- Orbital Bombardment: An intense siege where a faction rapidly bombards a defending station.\n- Distress Beacon Trap: A fake distress signal that ambushes the player.\n- Station Siege: Heavy siege ships attempt to tear down a station\'s defenses.\n- Sector Blockade: A heavily armed fleet establishes a lockdown over a sector.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a11', 'Dynamic Invasions & Scaling'%_t, 'Vanilla invasions spawn a static number of small ships. Cosmic War introduces advanced mathematical scaling:\n\n- Strength Matching: Invasions analyze the total combined Omicron and Volume of all defending stations and ships in the sector, dynamically adjusting the invading fleet\'s size and ship volume to match 100% of the defending force.\n- Siege Dreadnoughts: Large invasions spawn specialized Dreadnoughts with 5x shield multipliers to survive station point defense.\n- Shield Jamming (Surprise Attacks): Invasions have a 35% chance to deploy Electronic Warfare, instantly locking all defending shields (including players) to 0 for the first 20 seconds of the assault!\n- Cinematic Battlefield HUD: Entering a contested War Zone attaches a 100% split Red/Blue UI Bar to your screen, visually tracking the siege duration.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a12', 'Planetary Defense Generators'%_t, 'Primary file: data/scripts/entity/cw_planetary_defense.lua\n\nA massive defensive structure that can be constructed to protect sectors. While active, the Planetary Defense Generator projects an invincibility shield over all other allied stations in the sector, forcing invading fleets to destroy the generator first before they can assault the sector\'s core infrastructure.\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Strategic Checkpoints: Defenders can funnel invaders toward heavily fortified choke points.\n- Siege Mechanics: Attackers must break the planetary shield to successfully conquer a zone.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a13', 'Dynamic Faction Traits'%_t, 'Factions develop distinct personalities that dictate how they fight and negotiate.\n- Traits: Warmonger, Pacifist, Opportunist, Isolationist, Imperialist, Entrenched, Mercantile, Vengeful, and Xenophobic.\n- Impact: A Warmonger faction will constantly seek conflict and reject ceasefires, while a Mercantile faction will leverage trade embargoes and pay triple the standard rate for mercenary contracts.\n\nDormant Trait Revival: Cosmic War also reactivates 4 unused vanilla traits to add further nuance:\n- Active/Passive: Dictates how frequently a faction attempts territory expansions.\n- Strict/Forgiving: Modifies their likelihood to accept peace treaties or hold eternal grudges.\n- Smart/Dumb: Dictates their strategic intelligence when declaring wars against superior forces.\n- Sadistic/Sympathetic: Determines whether they offer bonus payouts, or severe penalties, for mercenaries destroying unarmed civilian ships.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a19', 'Galactic Politics Tab (UI)'%_t, 'Adds a fully featured, interactive intelligence UI tab to the Player Window, giving you unprecedented visibility into the macro-geopolitical state of the galaxy.\n\nKey Features:\n\n- Active Conflict Tracking: Displays a real-time, sortable list of all active AI wars, skirmishes, and ceasefires across the galaxy.\n- Interactive Column Sorting: Click any column header (Faction A, Faction B, War Heat, Status, Relations) to instantly sort ascending or descending.\n- Strategic Filtering: Filter the list by All, Active Conflicts, Ceasefires Only, or factions with Active Bounties.\n- Immersive Relation Toggle: Switch between raw numeric relation values and immersive diplomatic descriptors (e.g. "Allied", "Confrontational", "All-Out War").\n- Strategic Tooltips: Hovering over any conflict reveals internal Faction Indices, AI Traits, exact numerical player relations, and the exact credit payout of active War Bounties.\n- Dedicated Bounty Column: Active War Bounties get their own sortable column showing the credit reward at a glance.\n- Your License At A Glance: Your own active Bounty License (target, kills, time remaining) is shown right in the tab header.\n- Color-Coded Standing: Faction names are dynamically colored based on your personal reputation, so you can instantly spot when your allies are under attack.\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Transforms invisible background math into actionable intelligence, letting you hunt lucrative war bounties, intercept conflicts involving your allies, or identify volatile regions to exploit.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a20', 'War Casualties & Events'%_t, 'Injects immersive background events related to the ongoing galactic conflict, making the universe feel alive and reacting to the violence around you.\n\n- Refugee Convoys: Civilian ships fleeing warzones will occasionally hail you in deep space. Donating supplies or credits grants massive reputation boosts, and they have a 25% chance to upload the exact coordinates of a hidden resource stash directly to your galaxy map.\n- Distress Beacons: Wreckages of destroyed ships may broadcast an active distress signal. Interacting with the beacon to download logs and "Answer the Call" triggers a dynamic rescue (or ambush) scenario. Be warned: simply salvaging the wreck without answering the beacon permanently locks out the interaction!\n\nGameplay Impact:\n\n- Provides dynamic, narrative-driven events outside of standard missions.\n- Offers alternative, peaceful routes to gain massive faction standing via charity.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a21', 'Admin & Diagnostics Command'%_t, 'Command: /cosmicwarstatus\n\nProvides quick status and health visibility into the war simulation, including sanity checks for running servers. Useful for admins doing balancing or debugging on live servers.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a22', 'Bounty Board Command'%_t, 'Command: /cosmicwarbounties\n\nA quick chat-only summary of your own active War Bounty License (target faction, kill progress, time remaining), followed by a ranked list of every currently active War Bounty galaxy-wide with the offering faction, target faction, reward per kill, and time until expiry.\n\nUseful when you do not want to open the Galactic Politics tab just to check whether you still have an active License, or which factions are currently paying out the most.\n\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a14', 'Mercenary Contracts'%_t, 'Players can be hired directly by factions to participate in wars through the bulletin board. Contracts offer massive credit payouts and reputation boosts, but incur severe diplomatic penalties with the target faction.\n- Defensive Contracts: Guard key installations against sieges, or break blockades to deliver supplies (Blockade Runner).\n- Offensive Contracts: Participate in deep-strike operations and wipe out key enemy infrastructure (Sector Raid).\n- Special Operations: Deploy stealth buoys (Sensor Deployment), extract critical black box data (Black Box Retrieval), or draw massive enemy fleets into a 5-minute ambush (Distraction Carnage).\n- Resource Ops: Steal massive quantities of resources from enemy territory (Resource Heist) or destroy enemy mining operations (Resource Sabotage).\n- Assassination & Duels: Hunt down high-value targets, specialized fleets (Hunter Killer), or answer the call for a 1-on-1 duel with a massively scaled Champion (Champion Duel).\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c0', 'cw_cat_a15', 'Galactic Politics & Bounty Licenses'%_t, 'Players can influence the macro simulation and earn massive profits.\n- Bounty Licenses: Factions actively offering a Bounty License against their enemies show it in a dedicated Bounty column in the UI (or via /cosmicwarbounties). Destroying your first target activates a 45-minute hunting license for up to 15 kills, scaling with distance!\n- One License At A Time: You can only hold one active License at once. Check your current one anytime with /cosmicwarbounties or the Galactic Politics tab.\n- Covert Funding: Donate massive sums of credits to secretly fund rebellions and proxy wars against rival empires.\n- Bribes: Push factions toward ceasefires through heavy diplomatic investments.\n'%_t, '')

    -- Synergies & Integrations
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'cw_cat', 'cw_cat_c1', 'Synergies & Integrations'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c1', 'cw_cat_a16', 'Cosmic Vault Synergy'%_t, 'War heavily utilizes Vault APIs to spread its effects.\n- Deep Economy Warfare: Vault\'s Economy API allows sieges to cause massive famines in targeted sectors.\n- Weather-Assisted Boarding: AI troop transports use Vault Buffs to survive hazardous sectors while sieging.\n- Commodore Siege Leadership: AI Commodores spawn using Vault scaling APIs.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c1', 'cw_cat_a17', 'Synergy Updates'%_t, 'Interoperability with other Cosmic Mods.\n- Wartime Propaganda Beacons: War integrates with Chronicles Rumormonger system to spread propaganda.\n- Inherent Imperialism: Factions with the Imperialist trait will aggressively use Overhaul\'s siege logic to expand borders.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'cw_cat_c1', 'cw_cat_a18', 'Advanced Escalation & Rift DLC'%_t, 'Rift integration in late-game sieges.\n- Weaponized Subspace Tears: Extreme sieges can rip open Rift portals, spilling hazardous anomalies into real-space.\n- Dynamic Frontline Sieges & Subspace Containment Contracts: Rift missions blend with War bounties for massive payouts.\n- Alliance PvP Repercussions: Using Rift tech against players incurs severe diplomatic penalties.\n- Wartime Shortages: Blockades drastically limit Rift tech availability in standard markets.\n'%_t, '')

end
